🚨 2 Vulnerability(ies) Found

╭───────────── SKV-001 — Dynamic Installation of Untrusted Skills ─────────────╮
│  Category         :  REMOTE CODE EXECUTION / DYNAMIC CODE                    │
│  Severity         :  HIGH                                                    │
│                                                                              │
│  Affected Content :                                                          │
│    npx skills add <owner/repo@skill> -g -y                                   │
│                                                                              │
│  ⚠  Why it is vulnerable:                                                    │
│     The skill allows the installation of arbitrary skills from GitHub or     │
│  other sources using the 'npx skills add' command. If an attacker can        │
│  influence the owner/repo@skill parameter, they could potentially install    │
│  malicious code.                                                             │
│                                                                              │
│  🎯 Attack Scenario:                                                         │
│     An attacker could craft a query that includes a malicious skill URL.     │
│  For example, if the user asks to install a skill named'malicious-skill',    │
│  the agent would execute 'npx skills add malicious-skill'.                   │
│  If'malicious-skill' contains harmful code, it could lead to remote code     │
│  execution.                                                                  │
│                                                                              │
│  🛡  Remediation:                                                             │
│     Implement strict validation of the skill source and ensure that only     │
│  trusted repositories are allowed. Additionally, avoid installing skills     │
│  globally or skipping confirmation prompts.                                  │
╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
╭──────────── SKV-002 — External HTTP Requests for Skill Discovery ────────────╮
│  Category         :  DATA EXFILTRATION                                       │
│  Severity         :  MEDIUM                                                  │
│                                                                              │
│  Affected Content :                                                          │
│    npx skills find                                                           │
│                                                                              │
│  ⚠  Why it is vulnerable:                                                    │
│     The skill uses the 'npx skills find' command to search for skills        │
│  interactively or by keyword. This command makes HTTP requests to external   │
│  services to fetch skill information, which could potentially include        │
│  sensitive data.                                                             │
│                                                                              │
│  🎯 Attack Scenario:                                                         │
│     An attacker could manipulate the query to include sensitive information  │
│  in the HTTP request. If the skill sends this data to an external service,   │
│  it could be intercepted or logged, leading to data exfiltration.            │
│                                                                              │
│  🛡  Remediation:                                                             │
│     Ensure that all HTTP requests made by the skill are secured and do not   │
│  transmit sensitive data. Consider caching responses locally to reduce the   │
│  number of external requests.                                                │
╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
╭──────────────────────── 🚩 Dangerous Patterns Found ─────────────────────────╮
