🚨 2 Vulnerability(ies) Found

╭───────────────────── SKV-001 — Shell Command Execution ──────────────────────╮
│  Category         :  COMMAND/SHELL INJECTION                                 │
│  Severity         :  HIGH                                                    │
│                                                                              │
│  Affected Content :                                                          │
│    The setup instructions include shell commands that could be executed by   │
│  the agent.                                                                  │
│                                                                              │
│  ⚠  Why it is vulnerable:                                                    │
│     The setup instructions involve running shell commands like `gog auth     │
│  credentials /path/to/client_secret.json`. If an attacker can control the    │
│  `/path/to/client_secret.json`, they might inject malicious commands.        │
│                                                                              │
│  🎯 Attack Scenario:                                                         │
│     An attacker could modify the client_secret.json path to point to a       │
│  different location where they have placed a malicious script. When the      │
│  agent runs the command, it would execute the attacker's script instead of   │
│  the intended one.                                                           │
│                                                                              │
│  🛡  Remediation:                                                             │
│     Ensure that the path to the client_secret.json is securely managed and   │
│  cannot be altered by unauthorized users.                                    │
╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
╭──────── SKV-002 — Potential Data Exfiltration via OAuth Credentials ─────────╮
│  Category         :  DATA EXFILTRATION                                       │
│  Severity         :  MEDIUM                                                  │
│                                                                              │
│  Affected Content :                                                          │
│    The setup involves storing OAuth credentials which could potentially be   │
│  exfiltrated.                                                                │
│                                                                              │
│  ⚠  Why it is vulnerable:                                                    │
│     OAuth credentials stored in client_secret.json can be accessed by the    │
│  agent. If the agent is compromised, these credentials could be              │
│  exfiltrated, leading to potential data leakage.                             │
│                                                                              │
│  🎯 Attack Scenario:                                                         │
│     An attacker gains access to the agent and retrieves the OAuth            │
│  credentials stored in client_secret.json. They then use these credentials   │
│  to gain access to the Google Workspace services associated with the agent.  │
│                                                                              │
│  🛡  Remediation:                                                             │
│     Store OAuth credentials securely and limit access to them. Consider      │
│  using environment variables or secure vaults for storing sensitive          │
│  information.                                                                │
╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
