╭───────────────────────── 🎯 Skill Purpose Analysis ──────────────────────────╮
│  The skill is designed to provide a convenient way to summarize various      │
│  types of content. However, its reliance on external URLs and files, along   │
│  with the need for API keys, makes it inherently risky if not properly       │
│  secured.                                                                    │
╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯

🚨 3 Vulnerability(ies) Found

╭─────── SKV-001 — Summarization of URLs can lead to data exfiltration ────────╮
│  Category         :  DATA EXFILTRATION                                       │
│  Severity         :  HIGH                                                    │
│                                                                              │
│  Affected Content :                                                          │
│    bash                                                                      │
│  summarize "https://example.com" --model google/gemini-3-flash-preview       │
│                                                                              │
│                                                                              │
│  ⚠  Why it is vulnerable:                                                    │
│     The skill allows summarizing URLs, which can potentially include         │
│  sensitive information. If the URL points to a resource containing           │
│  confidential data, summarizing it could inadvertently transmit that data    │
│  outside the secure environment.                                             │
│                                                                              │
│  🎯 Attack Scenario:                                                         │
│     An attacker could provide a URL pointing to a document containing        │
│  sensitive information. The agent would then fetch and summarize the         │
│  content, potentially leaking sensitive data through the summarization       │
│  service.                                                                    │
│                                                                              │
│  🛡  Remediation:                                                             │
│     Restrict the URLs that can be summarized to trusted sources or ensure    │
│  that only public, non-sensitive URLs are processed.                         │
╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
╭─────────────── SKV-002 — Hardcoded API keys in configuration ────────────────╮
│  Category         :  CREDENTIAL / SECRET EXPOSURE                            │
│  Severity         :  HIGH                                                    │
│                                                                              │
│  Affected Content :                                                          │
│    - OpenAI: `OPENAI_API_KEY`                                                │
│  - Anthropic: `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`                                            │
│  - xAI: `XAI_API_KEY`                                                        │
│  - Google: `GEMINI_API_KEY` (aliases: `GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY`,        │
│  `GOOGLE_API_KEY`)                                                           │
│                                                                              │
│  ⚠  Why it is vulnerable:                                                    │
│     The skill requires setting API keys in the environment, which could be   │
│  hardcoded or stored insecurely. This exposes the risk of credential         │
│  leakage if the environment variables are not properly managed.              │
│                                                                              │
│  🎯 Attack Scenario:                                                         │
│     An attacker gains access to the environment where the skill runs and     │
│  retrieves the API keys, allowing them to make unauthorized API calls using  │
│  the stolen credentials.                                                     │
│                                                                              │
│  🛡  Remediation:                                                             │
│     Ensure that API keys are securely stored and never hardcoded in the      │
│  skill or environment variables. Use secure vaults or secrets management     │
│  solutions.                                                                  │
╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
╭───────────── SKV-003 — Processing of external content as input ──────────────╮
│  Category         :  INDIRECT / EMBEDDED INJECTION                           │
│  Severity         :  MEDIUM                                                  │
│                                                                              │
│  Affected Content :                                                          │
│    bash                                                                      │
│  summarize "/path/to/file.pdf" --model google/gemini-3-flash-preview         │
│                                                                              │
│                                                                              │
│  ⚠  Why it is vulnerable:                                                    │
│     The skill processes external files and URLs, which could contain         │
│  malicious content. If an attacker can control the input, they might inject  │
│  harmful content that gets processed by the summarization tool.              │
│                                                                              │
│  🎯 Attack Scenario:                                                         │
│     An attacker provides a crafted PDF or URL that contains malicious        │
│  content. When the agent summarizes the input, it could execute unintended   │
│  actions or leak sensitive data.                                             │
│                                                                              │
│  🛡  Remediation:                                                             │
│     Validate and sanitize all inputs before processing them with the         │
│  summarization tool. Ensure that only trusted and sanitized inputs are       │
│  allowed.                                                                    │
╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
